class Solution {
    int getMiddle(Node head) {
        if (head == null) {                    // Empty list check
            return 0;                          // Return 0 (or -1 for error)
        }

        int count = 0;                         // Counter for total nodes

        // First pass: count total nodes
        for (Node curr = head; curr != null; curr = curr.next) {
            count++;                           // Increment count for each node
        }

        Node newCur = head;                    // Pointer to find middle

        // Second pass: move to middle position (count/2)
        for (int i = 0; i < count / 2; i++) {
            newCur = newCur.next;              // Move forward
        }

        return newCur.data;                    // Return middle node's data
    }
}


//////////////////////// DRY RUN ////////////////////

List: 10 → 20 → 30 → 40 → 50

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

CASE 1: Odd Length (5 nodes)

INITIAL:
(head)
  │
  ▼
[10|•] → [20|•] → [30|•] → [40|•] → [50|•] → null

STEP 1: First pass - count nodes
  i=0: curr=10, count=1
  i=1: curr=20, count=2
  i=2: curr=30, count=3
  i=3: curr=40, count=4
  i=4: curr=50, count=5
  curr=null → stop

count = 5, middle index = 5/2 = 2

STEP 2: Second pass - move to index 2
  i=0: newCur = 20
  i=1: newCur = 30
  i=2: loop ends (i < 2 false)

FINAL:
(head)                (newCur)
  │                      │
  ▼                      ▼
[10|•] → [20|•] → [30|•] → [40|•] → [50|•] → null

Result: 30 (middle element)


━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

CASE 2: Even Length (4 nodes)

List: 10 → 20 → 30 → 40

INITIAL:
[10|•] → [20|•] → [30|•] → [40|•] → null

STEP 1: count = 4, middle index = 4/2 = 2

STEP 2: Move to index 2
  i=0: newCur = 20
  i=1: newCur = 30

FINAL:
[10|•] → [20|•] → [30|•] → [40|•] → null
                    ↑
                 newCur

Result: 30 (second middle element)


━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

CASE 3: Single Node

List: 7 → null

STEP 1: count = 1, middle index = 1/2 = 0

STEP 2: Loop doesn't run (i < 0 false), newCur stays at head

Result: 7


//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Middle of a Linked List
You are given the head of a linked list, You have to return the value of the middle node of the linked list.
If the number of nodes is odd, return the middle node value.
If the number of nodes is even, there are two middle nodes, so return the second middle node value.

Input : 10 → 20 → 30 → 40 → 50
Output: 30

Input : 10 → 20 → 30 → 40
Output: 30 (second middle for even length)

Input : 7
Output: 7

Input : null
Output: 0

Edge Cases:
1. Empty list → return 0
2. Single node → return that node's data
3. Odd length → return exact middle node
4. Even length → return second middle node (index = n/2)

Constraints:
• 1 ≤ size of linked list ≤ 10⁶
• 1 ≤ data of nodes ≤ 10⁶

TC: O(n) | SC: O(1)
